Subject: [PATCH 18/18] docs: document the touchscreen-swipe action options

Document the full touchscreen-swipe node set (previously only fingers
and off were listed): tap, tap-4, swipe-4-down/up, hold, and the new
horizontal-swipe mode, with their fallback rules. Add a Column Resize
entry to the gesture overview.
---
 docs/wiki/Configuration:-Gestures.md | 42 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 docs/wiki/Gestures.md                | 10 +++++++
 2 files changed, 52 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Gestures.md b/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Gestures.md
index 0d298feb..7c6f067c 100644
--- a/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Gestures.md
+++ b/docs/wiki/Configuration:-Gestures.md
@@ -32,6 +32,15 @@ gestures {
     touchscreen-swipe {
         fingers 3
         // off
+        // horizontal-swipe "resize-column"
+        // tap { maximize-column; }
+        // tap-4 { toggle-overview; }
+        // swipe-4-down { close-window; }
+        // swipe-4-up { spawn-sh "on-screen-keyboard"; }
+        // hold {
+        //     left { move-column-left; }
+        //     right { move-column-right; }
+        // }
     }
 
     // touchscreen-edge-swipe {
@@ -143,10 +152,43 @@ Three-finger swipe gestures on a touchscreen, replicating the touchpad behavior:
 
 The gesture uses the same continuous animation and inertia as the touchpad swipe.
 
+On top of the animated swipes, discrete actions can be bound to taps and specific
+swipe shapes, and the horizontal swipe can be switched to resize the focused
+window. Anything left unbound falls back to the animated gesture (or, for taps
+with four or more fingers, to the regular `tap` action).
+
 The options are:
 
 - `fingers`: number of fingers required to trigger the gesture (default: 3).
 - `off`: disable touchscreen swipe gestures entirely.
+- `horizontal-swipe`: what a quick horizontal swipe does (default:
+  `"move-view"`). `"resize-column"` makes the swipe resize the focused
+  window's width, tracking the fingers 1:1: dragging right widens it, dragging
+  left narrows it, and the width stays where the fingers leave it. Tiled: the
+  focused column; floating: the focused window. Without a focused window the
+  swipe falls back to moving the view.
+- `tap`: action for a quick tap with `fingers` fingers (default:
+  `maximize-column`). All fingers down and up within a short window, without
+  enough movement to become a swipe.
+- `tap-4`: action for taps involving four or more fingers; overrides `tap` for
+  those.
+- `swipe-4-down` / `swipe-4-up`: discrete action for a quick vertical swipe
+  with four or more fingers. Unset, such swipes drive the workspace carousel.
+- `hold { left/right/up/down { ... } }`: discrete actions for held swipes:
+  fingers resting still for a moment (~400ms) before swiping. A direction left
+  unset falls back to the animated swipe.
+
+```kdl
+gestures {
+    touchscreen-swipe {
+        // Example: horizontal swipes resize the focused window, a 4-finger
+        // tap opens the overview, a 4-finger flick down closes the window.
+        horizontal-swipe "resize-column"
+        tap-4 { toggle-overview; }
+        swipe-4-down { close-window; }
+    }
+}
+```
 
 ```kdl
 gestures {
diff --git a/docs/wiki/Gestures.md b/docs/wiki/Gestures.md
index 4655a856..c3475eab 100644
--- a/docs/wiki/Gestures.md
+++ b/docs/wiki/Gestures.md
@@ -77,6 +77,16 @@ The gesture uses the same continuous carousel animation as the touchpad.
 
 Move the view horizontally with three-finger horizontal swipes on the touchscreen.
 
+#### Column Resize
+
+<sup>Since: 26.04</sup>
+
+With `touchscreen-swipe { horizontal-swipe "resize-column" }`, horizontal
+swipes resize the focused window's width instead of moving the view: the width
+tracks the fingers 1:1 while swiping and stays where they leave it.
+
+See [`touchscreen-swipe`](./Configuration:-Gestures.md#touchscreen-swipe).
+
 #### Edge Swipes
 
